# Cursor Quick (Composer 2.5 Fast)

Temporary quick-task lane while the Cursor subscription lasts. `cursor-agent` is
installed at `~/.local/bin/cursor-agent` and already logged in — no API key needed.
`composer-2.5-fast` is Cursor's fast frontier model: good for quick bounded work, not
for judgment-heavy work.

## When to use

- Quick single-file edits, small scripts, scratch prototypes.
- Fast lookups, explanations, summaries where a fast second model saves Opus/Codex turns.
- Scouting — default scout lane per user 2026-07-06: repo/file lookups ("where is X
  defined", "what does Y do"), quick classification, single-question recon via the
  read-only ask-mode invocation below. Works on any directory (only writes need a git
  workspace). Multi-file agent-native sweeps stay on sonnet Explore/sonnet-scout;
  token-heavy digs (logs, giant specs) stay on `codex exec --sandbox read-only`.
- Docs and prose edits (README, guides, changelogs, PR/ticket text) — default docs lane
  per user 2026-07-06. Writes still need a git workspace; non-git config docs
  (~/.claude, ~/.codex, Desktop notes) stay inline with the Opus orchestrator.

## When NOT to use

- Security/auth/data/release work, architecture, multi-file refactors — Codex GPT-5.5 /
  opus lanes own those.
- Anything needing >~5 minutes: if it isn't quick, it isn't this lane.

## Invocation (verified against cursor-agent 2026.06.29)

Read-only (lookups / explain / plan):

```bash
timeout 300 cursor-agent -p --mode ask --model composer-2.5-fast --output-format text "<question>"
```

Quick write in a scratch dir or trivial repo edit (without `--force`, proposed edits are
NOT applied; `--trust` skips the headless workspace-trust prompt). Two smoke-verified
requirements: the workspace must be a **git repo** (`git init` a scratch dir first) and
pass `--sandbox disabled` — with a non-git dir and default sandbox, headless write runs
hang until timeout with no output:

```bash
timeout 300 cursor-agent -p --model composer-2.5-fast --output-format text --trust --force --sandbox disabled --workspace <git-dir> "<task>"
```

Repo edits that deserve isolation — builtin worktree at `~/.cursor/worktrees/<repo>/<name>`;
collect the diff from the worktree and integrate it yourself:

```bash
timeout 300 cursor-agent -p --model composer-2.5-fast --output-format text --trust --force --sandbox disabled -w <name> "<task>"
```

## Prompt style

Simple and goal-stated — no Claude-style scaffolding (same lesson as the Codex lane).
Include: "If you can't do this, say so plainly and name what you looked at" so an empty
result doesn't trigger a confused rerun.

## Guardrails

- Worker output is untrusted: verify edits (read the diff, run the check) before claiming
  done.
- Timeout = not-quick signal: on timeout, reroute to Codex (`codex-delegate.mjs`) or an
  opus worker instead of retrying here.
- EXPIRY 2026-07-22: when the Cursor sub lapses, delete `~/.codex/skills/cursor-quick`,
  the `~/.claude/skills/cursor-quick` symlink, and the dated "Cursor Composer" line in
  `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` Model Routing.
